# Data Layer (Remote + Local)

## Backend
- API: DummyJSON (`https://dummyjson.com`), docs: https://dummyjson.com/docs/products
- Base URL from `--dart-define=API_BASE_URL=...`, default `https://dummyjson.com` (`core/constant/api_constants.dart`).
- Endpoints used: `GET /products?limit&skip&select&sortBy&order` · `GET /products/search?q=&limit&select` · `GET /products/categories` · `GET /products/category/{slug}?limit&skip&select` · `GET /products/{id}`.
- Listing requests send `select=title,price,rating,category,brand,thumbnail` (`id` is implicit). Details use the full object.
- POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE are **simulated** by DummyJSON (not persisted). Never claim persistence.
- No price-range param exists → price filtering is local, pure, and unit-tested.

## Listing modes (reference §4.5.1)
- **Paged:** no search text and no price filter → "All" (`/products`) or category endpoint, `limit=20`, `skip`.
- **Full set:** search text or a price filter → one request with `limit=0` (`/products/search?q=` or `/products`), then `FilterPropertiesUseCase` applies category + price locally. Changing category/price never refetches; only a new search text does.
- The server can't combine search + category or filter by price. Don't send those params expecting them to work.
- Featured: `/products?sortBy=rating&order=desc&limit=<n>`.

## Remote data source
- Only class that touches `Dio`. Returns **models**, throws typed exceptions.
- Map `DioException`: `connectionTimeout|sendTimeout|receiveTimeout|transformTimeout` → `RequestTimeoutException`; `connectionError|badCertificate` (and `unknown` with `SocketException`) → `NetworkException`; `badResponse` → `ServerException(statusCode)`; `cancel` → `RequestCancelledException`; JSON/type errors → `ParsingException`; anything else → `UnknownException`. (Implemented in `core/network/dio_client.dart`.)
- Full-set calls (search, whole catalog) accept a pure-Dart `CancellationSignal` (`core/utils/cancellation_signal.dart`), so domain and presentation never import Dio. The remote data source converts it to a Dio `CancelToken`: an already cancelled signal throws `RequestCancelledException` without a request; cancelling in flight aborts it. Use one signal per request and cancel the previous one on every new query.
- Paged responses: `hasReachedMax` is `skip + limit >= total` from the response (DummyJSON echoes the returned count in `limit`).

## Local data source (reference §4.5.2)
- Backed by `SharedPreferences`. **Only two keys** (`StorageKeys.productsFirstPage`, `StorageKeys.categories`). Never add a key without approval.
- Envelope `{schemaVersion, cachedAt, data}`. Version mismatch or corrupt value → remove the key and throw `CacheException`.
- Bounds: first page = "All" page 0, ≤ 20 items, listing fields only; categories list; skip any write over 32 KB.
- Not persisted: details (in-memory only, last 20 in the session), Featured, pages > 0, category pages, search/full-set results, favorites (Q8 not approved).

## Repository strategy (in `*_repository_impl.dart`)
| Call | Strategy |
| --- | --- |
| "All" page 0 | Always remote when online → save → fresh. Fails with Network/Timeout/Server/UnexpectedResponse failure → cached page (< 24 h) with `isFromCache: true`; otherwise return that failure. 4xx never falls back |
| Pages > 0, category pages, search/full set, Featured | Remote only |
| Categories | In-memory → persisted (< 24 h) → remote → save; remote failure → stale persisted copy if any |
| Details | Remote → keep in memory; on failure, in-memory item, else the failure |
- Check `NetworkInfo.isConnected` before remote calls (connectivity only, not proof the API is reachable).
- Cache write failures never fail the request.
- Never call the network from widgets, `build()`, or `initState` without a Cubit.

## Models
- `fromJson` is defensive via `model/json_readers.dart`: wrong types, blank strings, and non-finite numbers (`NaN`, `Infinity`, overflowing literals such as `1e400`) become `null`/defaults; lists default to `const []`; nullable image URLs allowed. Every listing field may be missing (`select` omits absent keys such as `brand`).
- `toEntity()` maps API product → `PropertyEntity` (approved superset, reference §4.6). Never invent fields the API lacks. `weight`/`dimensions` aren't mapped; `stock`/`availabilityStatus` must never be shown as bedrooms, bathrooms, or area.
